# Docker build-context exclusions — applied at ``docker build`` time.
# Without this, ``COPY . .`` in the API + web Dockerfiles pulls in the
# repo's local ``node_modules`` (706MB+ from earlier pnpm runs) and
# ``.next`` build artifacts (580MB+), bloating the build context and
# overwriting freshly-installed dependencies inside the image. The
# latter caused ``next/dist/bin/next`` to vanish after install: the
# host's stale symlinked node_modules shadowed the freshly-installed
# hoisted one. See PR/issue notes for the symptom chain.

# Workspace-wide
**/node_modules
**/node_modules/**
.pnpm-store/
**/.pnpm-store

# Next.js build output
**/.next
**/.next/**
out/
**/out
**/out/**

# Python caches / build artifacts
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.eggs/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
htmlcov/
.coverage
*.egg-info/

# Local env / secrets — must NEVER reach a public image
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local
*.pem
*.key
*.crt

# Repo metadata that should never be in an image
.git/
.gitignore
.github/
.agent/
.taskmaster/
.claude/
.cursor/
.windsurfrules
.roomodes
.mcp.json
.vscode/

# OS / IDE noise
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
ehthumbs.db

# Local scripts that may pollute /app
docs/
scripts/dev/run.log